      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;How many syntax issues are there in the following code, and what are they?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;import (&#xA;    &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;)&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    var x string = nil&#xA;    if x == nil {&#xA;        x = &amp;#34;default&amp;#34;&#xA;    }&#xA;    fmt.Println(x)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;./prog.go:8:17: cannot use nil as string value in variable declaration&#xA;./prog.go:9:10: invalid operation: x == nil (mismatched types string and untyped nil)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;h3 class=&#34;heading-element&#34; id=&#34;var-x-string--nil-error&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;code&gt;var x string = nil&lt;/code&gt; Error&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;  &lt;a href=&#34;#var-x-string--nil-error&#34; class=&#34;heading-mark&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;svg class=&#34;octicon octicon-link&#34; viewBox=&#34;0 0 16 16&#34; version=&#34;1.1&#34; width=&#34;16&#34; height=&#34;16&#34; aria-hidden=&#34;true&#34;&gt;&lt;path d=&#34;m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z&#34;&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;In Go, the zero value for a &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt; type is an empty string &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;, not &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt;. &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt; is typically used for types like pointers, slices, maps, channels, and interfaces. Therefore, assigning &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt; to a &lt;code&gt;string&lt;/code&gt; type variable &lt;code&gt;x&lt;/code&gt; will result in a compilation error.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 154</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_154/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 07 Jan 2025 11:47:02 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_154/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;What is the output of the following code?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func main() {&#xA;    i := 65&#xA;    fmt.Println(string(i))&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. A&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. 65&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;A &lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/lYfJ6qOVMJV&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;string(i)&lt;/code&gt;: In Go, &lt;code&gt;string(int)&lt;/code&gt; interprets the integer as a Unicode code point and returns the corresponding character.&#xA;65 is the ASCII code (and Unicode code point) for the character &amp;lsquo;A&amp;rsquo;, so &lt;code&gt;string(65)&lt;/code&gt; results in the string &amp;ldquo;A&amp;rdquo;.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/details&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Go Daily Question 148</title>
      <link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_148/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 01 Jan 2025 13:08:46 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_148/</guid>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category>
      <category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Which of the following options is correct?&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;package main&#xA;&#xA;import &amp;#34;fmt&amp;#34;&#xA;&#xA;func main() {&#xA;    str := &amp;#34;hello&amp;#34;&#xA;    str[0] = &amp;#39;x&amp;#39;&#xA;    fmt.Println(str)&#xA;}&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;A. hello&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;B. xello&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;C. compilation error&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;details&gt;&#xA;  &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p&gt;C&#xA;&lt;a href=&#34;https://go.dev/play/p/WKuFSxIZZM8&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Run online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://golang.google.cn/ref/spec#String_types&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;external nofollow noopener noreferrer&#34;&gt;Go Official Documentation - String Types&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Strings are immutable: once created, it is impossible to change the contents of a string.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;In the problem, &lt;code&gt;str&lt;/code&gt; is a string, and its content cannot be changed, so &lt;code&gt;str[0] = &#39;x&#39;&lt;/code&gt; will cause an error.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
